From: M1892 mainline bring-up <m1892@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mm: bypass kfree_rcu sheaf fast path on M1892

The 7.1-rc1 M1892 kernel produced a delayed fatal Oops in
__rcu_free_sheaf_prepare().  The failing sheaf contained the address of
rcu_free_sheaf itself as an object, consistent with stale or multiply queued
sheaf state.  Keep CONFIG_KVFREE_RCU_BATCHED and its established page/list
batching, but bypass the newer SLUB sheaf shortcut until the upstream sheaf
lifecycle is resolved or the product kernel is rebased.

This trades a small amount of kfree_rcu throughput for stability.  It does
not make kvfree_rcu synchronous and does not change ordinary SLUB allocation.

--- a/mm/slab_common.c
+++ b/mm/slab_common.c
@@ -1596,6 +1596,12 @@ static bool kfree_rcu_sheaf(void *obj)
 {
 	struct kmem_cache *s;
 	struct slab *slab;
+
+	/*
+	 * M1892 7.1-rc1: delayed invalid object in rcu_free_sheaf().
+	 * Retain the older kfree_rcu bulk/list batching below this shortcut.
+	 */
+	return false;
 
 	if (is_vmalloc_addr(obj))
 		return false;
